.TH "EPX\-SEGMENTS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-segments \- read and change customer segments and what is assigned to them
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments [flags]
epx segments [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes customer segments, which group customers to offer them items such as products or categories, and what is assigned to them: customers, IAM groups and items.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR. Its writes require the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx segments all\-items"
List the items of every segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments all\-items [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the items assigned to every segment, products or categories (TYPE), with their SEGMENT.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, SEGMENT, TYPE, CODE, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx segments bulk\-create"
Create segments in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments bulk\-create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the segments in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of segments, each as create takes it.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments bulk\-delete"
Delete segments in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments bulk\-delete [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the segments whose IDs \fB\-\-file\fR gives, a JSON array such as \fB["s1", "s2"]\fR. Emporix refuses to delete a segment that has items or customers assigned to it (400 Bad Request, exit 1) unless \fB\-\-with\-assignments\fR deletes those assignments with it. It deletes the IAM group assignments of a segment with it either way: a segment with only IAM groups assigned is deleted without \fB\-\-with\-assignments\fR. Emporix answers an unknown ID as one that it deleted (204 No Content).
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Deletes the segments that \fB\-\-file\fR names with one request, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type the tenant at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-assignments\fR
Delete the item and customer assignments of a segment with it (its IAM group assignments go either way).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments bulk\-update"
Upsert segments in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments bulk\-update [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the segments in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of segments, each with its id, or creates those that do not exist (an upsert).
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments create"
Create a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the segment in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object such as \fBepx segments get ID \-o json\fR prints one, with its name, siteCode, validity and status (INACTIVE unless it says ACTIVE); Emporix makes its id unless the body gives one. A segment with that id that exists already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments customers"
Read and change the customers of a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers [flags]
epx segments customers [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the customers assigned to a segment, personal data included, and assigns and removes them, for B2B with their legal entity.
.PP
Its reads require the customersegment.segment_read scope. Its writes require the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.SS "epx segments customers bulk\-delete"
Delete customer assignments of a segment in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers bulk\-delete SEGMENT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Removes the customers in \fB\-\-file\fR from the segment SEGMENT_ID, a JSON array such as \fB[{"customerId": "c1", "legalEntityId": "le1"}]\fR (without legalEntityId for B2C).
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Deletes the customer assignments of a segment that \fB\-\-file\fR names with one request, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type SEGMENT_ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments customers bulk\-update"
Upsert customer assignments of a segment in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers bulk\-update SEGMENT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Assigns the customers in \fB\-\-file\fR to the segment SEGMENT_ID, or replaces their assignments (an upsert): a JSON array of assignments, each with its customerId, for B2B its legalEntityId, and optionally its mixins and metadata. A segment holds customers without a legal entity (B2C) or with one (B2B), never both: Emporix refuses to assign one of the other kind.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments customers delete"
Remove a customer from a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers delete SEGMENT_ID CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Removes the customer CUSTOMER without a legal entity (B2C) from the segment SEGMENT_ID; Emporix answers one that is not assigned as removed. SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows, and CUSTOMER the customer\(aqs id (the id of \fBepx customers get NUMBER \-o json\fR), not its NUMBER.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type CUSTOMER at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx segments customers delete\-b2b"
Remove a customer of a legal entity from a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers delete\-b2b SEGMENT_ID CUSTOMER LEGAL_ENTITY [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Removes the customer CUSTOMER of the legal entity LEGAL_ENTITY (B2B) from the segment SEGMENT_ID; Emporix answers one that is not assigned as removed. SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows, CUSTOMER the customer\(aqs id (the id of \fBepx customers get NUMBER \-o json\fR), not its NUMBER, and LEGAL_ENTITY the ID that \fBepx legal\-entities list\fR shows.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type LEGAL_ENTITY at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx segments customers get"
Show one customer of a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers get SEGMENT_ID CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads one customer assigned to a segment without a legal entity (B2C), personal data included; one assigned with a legal entity (B2B) is not found (exit 4): get\-b2b reads it. SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found. CUSTOMER is the CUSTOMER that \fBepx segments customers list SEGMENT_ID\fR shows; an unknown one is not found. CUSTOMER is the customer\(aqs id, not the NUMBER that \fBepx customers get\fR takes; ASSIGNMENT is MANUAL or AUTOMATIC.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, NAME, EMAIL, LEGAL ENTITY, ASSIGNMENT.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx segments customers get\-b2b"
Show one customer of a legal entity in a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers get\-b2b SEGMENT_ID CUSTOMER LEGAL_ENTITY [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads one customer assigned to a segment with a legal entity (B2B), personal data included. SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found. CUSTOMER and LEGAL_ENTITY are the CUSTOMER and LEGAL ENTITY that \fBepx segments customers list SEGMENT_ID\fR shows; an unknown one is not found. CUSTOMER is the customer\(aqs id, not the NUMBER that \fBepx customers get\fR takes; ASSIGNMENT is MANUAL or AUTOMATIC.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, NAME, EMAIL, LEGAL ENTITY, ASSIGNMENT.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx segments customers list"
List the customers of a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers list SEGMENT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the customers of a segment (for B2B, with their legal entity), personal data included. list and search sort by id unless \fB\-\-sort\fR says otherwise, an order that Emporix keeps across pages: unsorted, it pages them in a different order per request. SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows; an unknown one lists nothing. CUSTOMER is the customer\(aqs id, not the NUMBER that \fBepx customers get\fR takes; ASSIGNMENT is MANUAL or AUTOMATIC.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_read scope.
.PP
