Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx segments customers search"
Search the customers of a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers search SEGMENT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the customers of a segment that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every one), personal data included. list and search sort by id unless \fB\-\-sort\fR says otherwise, an order that Emporix keeps across pages: unsorted, it pages them in a different order per request. It reads and shows them as \fBepx segments customers list SEGMENT_ID\fR does. SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows; an unknown one lists nothing.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole. CUSTOMER is the customer\(aqs id, not the NUMBER that \fBepx customers get\fR takes; ASSIGNMENT is MANUAL or AUTOMATIC.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, NAME, EMAIL, LEGAL ENTITY, ASSIGNMENT.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx segments customers update"
Assign a customer to a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers update SEGMENT_ID CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Assigns the customer CUSTOMER without a legal entity (B2C) to the segment SEGMENT_ID, or replaces its assignment (an upsert). SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows, and CUSTOMER the customer\(aqs id (the id of \fBepx customers get NUMBER \-o json\fR), not its NUMBER. A segment holds customers without a legal entity (B2C) or with one (B2B), never both: Emporix refuses to assign one of the other kind. \fB\-\-file\fR may give the assignment\(aqs mixins and metadata (its version and the schemas of its mixins); without it, epx sends an empty object. Send its metadata.version as read to change it only if nobody changed it since: Emporix answers 409 Conflict (exit 5) otherwise.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx segments customers update\-b2b"
Assign a customer of a legal entity to a segment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx segments customers update\-b2b SEGMENT_ID CUSTOMER LEGAL_ENTITY [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Assigns the customer CUSTOMER of the legal entity LEGAL_ENTITY (B2B) to the segment SEGMENT_ID, or replaces its assignment (an upsert). SEGMENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx segments list\fR shows, CUSTOMER the customer\(aqs id (the id of \fBepx customers get NUMBER \-o json\fR), not its NUMBER, and LEGAL_ENTITY the ID that \fBepx legal\-entities list\fR shows. A segment holds customers without a legal entity (B2C) or with one (B2B), never both: Emporix refuses to assign one of the other kind. \fB\-\-file\fR may give the assignment\(aqs mixins and metadata (its version and the schemas of its mixins); without it, epx sends an empty object. Send its metadata.version as read to change it only if nobody changed it since: Emporix answers 409 Conflict (exit 5) otherwise.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the customersegment.segment_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
